        "rapidmlx/qwen3.8:27b",
        "--title",
        "comparison launch",
        "Add a maxAliases loader option to load() and loadAll(), documented in README next to the other load options, that limits how many alias nodes (*ref) a single document may contain. The default -1 means no limit; 0 rejects any alias; a positive N allows at most N alias uses per document. Exceeding the limit must throw the library's YAMLException with a message containing \"maxAliases\" (for example \"aliases exceeded maxAliases (1)\"). The count resets for every document in a multi-document stream, so loadAll on two documents with one alias each succeeds with maxAliases: 1 and fails with maxAliases: 0. Documents without aliases are unaffected whatever the option. Source is under src/ (TypeScript); the package is built with npm run build and tests run with node --test \"test/core/**/*.test.mjs\" \"test/spec/*.test.mjs\".\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npm run build && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: node --test test/core/**/*.test.mjs test/spec/*.test.mjs\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/."
      ],
